\procedure kanban-card()
<div style="padding:0.4em 0.6em;margin-bottom:0.4em;border:1px solid #888;border-radius:3px;background:#f6f6f6;color:#222;"><$text text=<<currentTiddler>>/></div>
\end

<<.from-version "5.5.0">> The <<.def make-live-reorderable-list>> [[procedure|Procedures]] renders a list whose items the user can put in a different order by dragging them. The order is shown as it is being chosen: the other items move aside as the dragged one passes, so that what is on the screen is always what the list will look like if it is dropped there. See DragAndDropMechanism for an overview.

It is used by the story river and by the "Open" tab of the sidebar.

The procedure renders three things: the items themselves, an AnimateLayoutWidget so that items settle into their new places rather than jumping, and a drop target covering the whole list so that a drop between the items still lands. The two procedures it uses for those, <<.def make-live-reorderable>> and <<.def make-live-reorder-backstop>>, are described separately and are not normally used on their own.

!! Parameters

|!Parameter |!Description |
|list |Title of the tiddler whose ''list'' field holds the order being shown and changed |
|content |The markup for a single item, usually a procedure. It is rendered once per item with <<.vlink currentTiddler>> set to that item |
|commit |When to write the new order: `live` (the default) changes the list as the drag proceeds, `drop` assembles the order in the drag state and writes it to the list only when the item is dropped |
|dragState |Title of the tiddler holding the state of the drag (defaults to `$:/state/tiddlywiki/live-reorder`). Each list needs its own, so pass a title made with the <<.mlink qualify>> macro if the list can appear more than once |
|enable |Optional value "no" to switch dragging and dropping off, leaving the list rendered as usual. Left unset, the list follows the <<.var tv-enable-drag-and-drop>> variable, which carries the reader's own setting for drag and drop; giving a value here decides the matter for this list whatever that setting says |
|group |Optional name of a group of lists that exchange items. Lists given the same group share the state of a drag, which is what lets an item dragged out of one of them be carried into another. Left blank, the list keeps its items to itself |
|transfer |What becomes of an item carried out of this list: `move` (the default) takes it out, `copy` leaves it behind. It describes only what happens to the list the drag started in, since an item carried on from a list it was dropped into is always moved |
|acceptDrops |Optional value "yes" to let items dragged from elsewhere be dropped into the list, which inserts them at the place they are dropped (defaults to "no"). The "Open" tab of the sidebar uses this, so that dragging a tiddler title into it opens that tiddler at that position |
|dropActions |Optional actions to be performed after an item has been dropped |
|class |Optional CSS classes to assign to each item |
|history |Optional title of the history tiddler, passed to the ListWidget |
|storyview |Optional name of the storyview module that animates changes to the list, passed to the ListWidget |
|emptyMessage |Optional message to show when the list is empty, passed to the ListWidget |
|duration |Optional length of the settling animation in milliseconds (defaults to {{$:/config/DragAndDrop/animation/duration}}) |
|easing |Optional easing of the settling animation (defaults to the value of `$:/config/DragAndDrop/animation/easing`) |
|direction |`vertical` (the default) if the items are stacked one above another, or `horizontal` if they sit side by side. It decides whether an item is split into a top and a bottom half or a left and a right one |
|itemDisplay |Optional CSS `display` value for each item (defaults to `flow-root`) |
|ghostOpacity |Optional opacity of the item being dragged (defaults to `0.3`) |
|styleZIndex |Optional `z-index` for the drop targets (defaults to `501`) |

!! Where it can be rendered

<<.warning """Render it with `$mode="inline"`. Rendered in block mode the items are wrapped in a paragraph, which puts them in a different element from the drop target that covers the list.""">>

The element the list is laid out in must be positioned, meaning it must have a CSS `position` other than `static`, because the drop target that covers the list is placed against it. Nothing else should be rendered between that element and the items, so that the items are drawn on top of that drop target rather than beneath it.

<<.warning "A list that accepts drops keeps its drop targets at all times, not only while one of its own items is being dragged. Those targets take the drop in place of anything behind them, including the DropzoneWidget that imports tiddlers dragged in from outside the window, so it is worth switching on only where the list is a small enough part of the page for that not to matter.">>

!! Examples

!!! Reordering one list

```
\procedure my-item()
<div class="my-item"><$text text=<<currentTiddler>>/></div>
\end

<div style="position: relative;">
<$transclude $variable="make-live-reorderable-list" $mode="inline"
	list="$:/StoryList" content=<<my-item>> dragState=<<qualify "$:/state/my-list">>/>
</div>
```

!!! Several lists that exchange items

Giving a number of lists the same <<.param group>> lets a card be dragged out of any of them and into any other. Each column is positioned, as the list requires, and lays its cards out one below another. The whole board is positioned too, and carries a drop target of its own, so that the space between the columns still counts as being on the board:

<$let board-todo="$:/temp/kanban/todo" board-doing="$:/temp/kanban/doing" board-done="$:/temp/kanban/done">

<$button>
<$action-listops $tiddler=<<board-todo>> $field="list" $filter="Sketch Spec Icons Palette Copy Layout Tests"/>
<$action-listops $tiddler=<<board-doing>> $field="list" $filter="Header Sidebar Search Print Import Export Backup"/>
<$action-listops $tiddler=<<board-done>> $field="list" $filter="Fonts Colours Spacing Margins"/>
Set up the board
</$button>

<div style="position:relative;">
<$transclude $variable="make-live-reorder-backstop" $mode="inline" group="kanban"/>
<div style="display:flex;gap:1em;align-items:flex-start;">
<div style="flex:1;position:relative;">
''To do''
<$transclude $variable="make-live-reorderable-list" $mode="inline" list=<<board-todo>> content=<<kanban-card>> group="kanban"/>
</div>
<div style="flex:1;position:relative;">
''Doing''
<$transclude $variable="make-live-reorderable-list" $mode="inline" list=<<board-doing>> content=<<kanban-card>> group="kanban"/>
</div>
<div style="flex:1;position:relative;">
''Done''
<$transclude $variable="make-live-reorderable-list" $mode="inline" list=<<board-done>> content=<<kanban-card>> group="kanban"/>
</div>
</div>
</div>

</$let>

<<.warning """A board of grouped lists needs that <<.dlink make-live-reorder-backstop "make-live-reorder-backstop Procedure">> over the whole of it. Without it the space between the columns belongs to no list, and a drag crossing that space is taken for a drag that has left the board altogether, which puts the card back where it came from in the middle of being dragged. The more columns there are, the more such space there is to cross.""">>

<<.tip """Add `transfer="copy"` to a column and cards dragged out of it are left behind rather than taken away, which is how a column of things to pick from rather than to move is built.""">>

<<.warning """A group needs `commit="live"`. The order assembled for a deferred commit is kept in one field of the drag state, which has no room for the several lists a group involves.""">>
